# test debris
JWT_AUTH_GUIDE.md

# This dev machine's own opencode install and npm cache. NOTHING here belongs in
# the repo - `skills/` at the root is the source, and setup.sh links from there
# into each project. A second copy under .opencode/ is worse than redundant:
# opencode reads .opencode/skills/ from whatever directory it is started in, so a
# stale copy in the clone silently outranks the real one. That happened - the
# tracked copy was the pre-cleanup coordinator playbook with the old gate, plus a
# symlink to a directory deleted in the same cleanup, broken in every clone.
.opencode/
.npm/

# credential registry: machine-specific, regenerated by `fa bootstrap`
state/
